From: batya <batya@github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 19:31:05 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 11/16] feat(ui): the window reads its sessions from the
 service, and each queue remembers its mode

Sessions moved to the database, so the window asks for them: the session list,
the number of tracks in a session, and the session a track belongs to all come
from the service, and a track that appears is written into the open session.
Where sessions and their tracks were kept in local storage before, nothing of
that is left.

How a queue plays back is read when the context opens and written back when the
player's buttons change it, so a session, a playlist or the library each come
back with the repeat mode and shuffle they were left with.
